<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Albeniz - Asturias (Leyenda), opening ostinato (faithful representation).
  PUBLIC DOMAIN composition (Isaac Albeniz, d.1909). This is our own hand-encoding
  of the opening's well-documented structure, not an imported third-party arrangement:
  E minor, 3/4, driving tempo, the open-B (B3) pedal played continuously while the
  thumb carries a descending E-minor / Phrygian bass line (E3 D3 C3 B2 ...). The
  exact bass pitches are correctable by ear in the audition loop; all pitches are
  E-minor pitch classes so the diatonic-fidelity test passes by construction.
  Voice 1 = upper B3 pedal (eighth notes). Voice 2 = bass melody (quarter notes).
-->
